{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_20_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_service", "label": "ecs-rds-postgres-pool Service Plan (Plan 1)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Status complete 2026-09-20: 13 tasks implemented and reviewed, 133 tests green with no database/AWS/collector; deliberately touches no Terraform and no AWS."}, {"id": "service_config_loadconfig", "label": "config.js loadConfig()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixes the environment-variable contract between plan 1 (service) and plan 2 (infrastructure); DATABASE_URL is required and throws, POOL_MAX defaults to 5 (knob 1), REPORT_SCAN_ROWS defaults to 0 so an uncalibrated service never silently runs a workload nobody chose."}, {"id": "service_prisma_schema", "label": "prisma/schema.prisma \u2014 Feed and Post models", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rejected an earlier single (pk, sk) table port of the DynamoDB access pattern on 2026-09-20 because it would never exercise a join, foreign key or a planner that can choose badly; Int (not BigInt) ids avoid JSON.stringify throwing on serialization."}, {"id": "service_context_asynclocalstorage", "label": "context.js runInRequestContext / currentRequest", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exists for one reason: pool checkout happens deep inside Prisma's call stack with no parameter to thread a route through, and without it a pool-wait histogram is process-global \u2014 able to say a queue existed but not whose requests were in it."}, {"id": "service_pool_instrumentconnect", "label": "pool.js createPool / instrumentConnect", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Highest-risk code in the plan: must never leak a connection and must distinguish a real queue from a brand-new physical connection being established (via pool.totalCount rising across the call), the spec's C3 contaminant."}, {"id": "service_db_createrepo", "label": "db.js createRepo \u2014 the four one-statement queries", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exactly one SQL statement per route is enforced by test assertion because the capacity model (pool of 5 \u00f7 20ms hold time = 250 rps) is only true at one checkout per request; the report route uses a single data-modifying CTE (scan\u2192aggregate\u2192insert) rather than pg_sleep, since sleeping would leave DBLoadCPU near zero and make the calibration target unreadable."}, {"id": "service_otel_starttelemetry", "label": "otel.js startTelemetry \u2014 pool wait histogram and gauges", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "db.pool.wait.duration is 'THE metric this project exists to produce'; its bucket boundaries are deliberately tighter at the low end than the request histogram's, and the three pool gauges (waiting/idle/total) are only registered once an OTLP exporter is actually running, so tests can assert no-op behavior with no collector."}, {"id": "service_handlers_routeclass", "label": "handlers.js matchRoute / ROUTE_CLASS / createHandlers", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ROUTE_CLASS is the single source of truth for route-to-latency-class mapping and must agree with slo.yaml's classes block in both directions, so a renamed route fails the build instead of silently leaving traffic unclassified."}, {"id": "service_server_createserver", "label": "server.js createServer / main()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately has no admission control (unlike the sibling's shedding) because shedding 429s would stop a saturated pool from ever producing the 5xx this project wants to measure; pool.warm() runs before listen() so no measured request pays for connection establishment."}, {"id": "service_seed_seedall", "label": "prisma/seed.js seedAll / buildFeeds / buildPostBatch", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deterministic and keyed off a fixed EPOCH rather than Date.now(), so created_at ordering (and therefore feed-route results) is identical across environments; VACUUM ANALYZE runs after seeding because an unanalyzed table gives the first session run a different query plan than the second."}, {"id": "service_slo_yaml", "label": "slo.yaml \u2014 SLI/SLO source of truth", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Class thresholds (fast/standard/heavy) are deliberately left null in plan 1, frozen only in plan 3 after calibration on the real instance, because they drive k6 VU sizing and inventing them early would be inventing the assertion the project exists to test."}, {"id": "service_generateslo_validateslo", "label": "generate-slo.js validateSlo / renderCapacityAdvisory", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "renderCapacityTfvars (RCU/WCU) is deleted with no Postgres analogue and replaced by a printable capacity advisory naming pool size \u00d7 task count vs. max_connections_estimate; a null-threshold guard makes npm run slo:check exit non-zero on purpose until plan 3."}, {"id": "service_calibrate_searchscanrows", "label": "scripts/calibrate.js searchScanRows", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pure binary search exported separately from its CLI wrapper so it can be tested without a database; the CLI caps its search ceiling at config.seedRows because the scan can't read more rows than the seed created, avoiding a false 'convergence' above the table size."}, {"id": "service_dockerfile", "label": "Dockerfile \u2014 multi-stage build", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "prisma generate runs at build time so the container needs no network or database to start; explicit --platform build avoids the arm64/amd64 CannotPullContainerError the sibling README records."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_20_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_service", "label": "Service plan (2026-09-20, plan 1)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md"}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_20_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_service", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_09_19_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_design", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "service_context_asynclocalstorage", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_d7_pool_wait_source", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.9}, {"source": "service_pool_instrumentconnect", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_d7_pool_wait_source", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.9}, {"source": "service_pool_instrumentconnect", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_c3_wait_contamination", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.9}, {"source": "service_db_createrepo", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_c1_pool_binding_constraint", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.9}, {"source": "service_calibrate_searchscanrows", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_d3_pool_binding", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.85}, {"source": "service_seed_seedall", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_c7_working_set_ram", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.85}, {"source": "service_server_createserver", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_d4_migrations_seed", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.85}, {"source": "service_prisma_schema", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_d6_fork_depth", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.85}, {"source": "service_slo_yaml", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_d1_sli", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.85}, {"source": "service_pool_instrumentconnect", "target": "service_context_asynclocalstorage", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-service.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "service_server_createserver", "target": "service_context_asynclocalstorage", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "sou